ins  we saw blood on the street it was a very  scary situation but we we thought that  it was best to run away and let the  first responders come in  and when did you feel safe where did you  go to  i went to my mother-in-law's house who  was about five minutes away and we  stayed there for about four or five  hours  because he was still on the loose nobody  knew where he was he was just described  as 18 to 20 year old white male which  could be a lot of people in the  community so we were scared and once we  knew that he was caught  then we went home and then late last  night my son woke up with a horrific  nightmare saying someone's killing me  someone's trying to kill me and he  started shaking so this nightmare is  just starting  yeah do you think this will change at  anything warren in terms of of the the  round the discourse about gun regulation  in america  i i see it more than just the gun  regulation this person could have had a  bomb this person had a gun i look at it  from those with neurological disorders  like myself i have a condition called  dyspraxia why did this person  who struggled who ended up dropping out  of high school who had problems in the  community not get to support and me and  my kids with dyspraxia are getting the  help within our ieps what made him do  this this is what we want to know as a  family is how we can make sure nobody  else feels so horrible they have to  shoot down our innocent victims  and the news that it was a local man  what impact does that does that have on  the community that it was somebody from  within your own community that was doing  this  very scary that it's it could be  homegrown it's also very fearful that  this child  now an adult in his 20s wasn't supported  why did he get to this point  what did they lack within our community  that we can help and improve so another  child who becomes a teen or adult  doesn't feel so angry that he has to  attack innocent people
 

